---
const profiles = [
  ['Portable spec', 'Frontmatter compliance against pinned upstream fixtures'],
  ['Host compatibility', 'Portable and Copilot extensions kept separate'],
  ['Information architecture', 'Resource graph, pointers, disclosure, and workflow criteria'],
  ['Behavioral evidence', 'Observed routing, task assertions, trajectories, and lift'],
  ['Safety & supply chain', 'Containment, scripts, locks, permissions, and limits'],
  ['Lifecycle health', 'Ownership, eval coverage, mirrors, versions, and releases'],
];
---

<section class="py-24 md:py-32 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-light-gray">
      Six profiles. No misleading composite grade.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mid-gray text-lg max-w-3xl">
      Every finding states its basis and evidence level. Missing observations
      stay unknown instead of becoming a pass.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-mid-gray/10">
      {profiles.map(([name, description], index) => (
        <div class="bg-dark-gray p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-orange-accent">
            {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
          </span>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-light-gray">{name}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mid-gray leading-relaxed">{description}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 bg-dark-gray border-l-2 border-orange-accent p-6">
      <code class="text-light-gray">pass · fail · warning · unknown · not-applicable</code>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mid-gray">
        Evidence advances from declared to statically verified, executed,
        baseline compared, and independently reproduced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
